<h1 class="article-title">Infrastructure Construction to Begin at Liepāja Industrial Park</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>Within the next month, the Liepāja SEZ Authority will start the first construction works to transform the former Liepājas Metalurgs steelworks site into a modern Liepāja Industrial Park based on circular-economy principles. Three procurement procedures for the first new street sections have now been completed, and an agreement on electrification of the area through new modern electricity networks has been approved. Construction is scheduled for completion by 31 December 2025. This will partially open the formerly closed factory territory to the public and allow the first investors to be attracted.</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority has approved the procurement results for the first street construction works under Phase I of the “Development of Liepāja Industrial Park Infrastructure” project. Work will begin within the next month to transform the former Liepājas Metalurgs factory into a modern green industrial park and begin opening the area to public access. Following procurement, A-Land will implement stage 1.1 for EUR 1.6 million and stage 1.3 for EUR 1.85 million, while SIA CTB will carry out stage 2.1 for EUR 2.8 million. All three street sections will receive utility networks, including water supply, domestic sewerage, stormwater drainage and district heating. AS Sadales tīkls will also begin building electricity supply infrastructure in parallel with the street works.</p><p>Phase I of the “Development of Liepāja Industrial Park Infrastructure” project is being implemented with EUR 10 million in funding from the Recovery and Resilience Facility.</p><p>Liepāja Industrial Park is being developed by the Liepāja SEZ Authority and Liepāja City Municipality on the former Liepājas metalurgs site between Brīvības, Meldru, Ezermalas, Parka and Zemnieku streets. It borders Lake Liepāja, a protected NATURA 2000 site. The objective is to create a modern business environment that attracts innovative, technologically advanced businesses and encourages the production of high-value-added goods in line with the European Green Deal and environmentally friendly circular-economy principles. According to the approved strategy, the plan is to attract over EUR 275 million in private investment and create at least 1,500 jobs.</p><p> </p><p>For reference:</p><ul><li>In 2018, the Ministry of Economics, the Investment and Development Agency of Latvia, SIA FeLM, Liepāja City Council and the Liepāja SEZ Authority signed a memorandum of intent on the development of the former Liepājas metalurgs site.</li><li>In 2021, the development programme for the former Liepājas metalurgs site was approved, and an interinstitutional agreement on its implementation was concluded with Liepāja City Council.</li><li>In 2022, the local spatial plan for the former Liepājas metalurgs site was approved.</li><li>In 2022, a remediation programme for the former Liepājas metalurgs site was developed.</li><li>In 2023, the Liepāja Industrial Park (LIP) Development Strategy for 2023–2028 was approved.</li><li>In 2023, several construction designs for the development of the area’s infrastructure were prepared.</li><li>In 2023, a project application for the first street construction works in the park was prepared and submitted, and confirmation of funding was received.</li><li>In 2023, a lease agreement was concluded with SIA Liepājas Steel until 31 December 2025 for the dismantling and removal of the electric steelmaking furnace.</li><li>At the end of 2023, an agreement was concluded with the Central Finance and Contracting Agency on EUR 10 million in Recovery and Resilience Facility funding for Phase I of the Liepāja Industrial Park infrastructure development project.</li></ul></div>
